and the quoting control runs bash with no login profile (#1187)\n\nThe landing review of 1187bl (run landing-over-an-existing-branch--5b5ccd50,\nREVIEW-REFORGE-EXHAUSTED-MEDIUM at d44ff0e95) raised two MEDIUMs, both in\ntest code, fixed here by hand under the operator's standing ruling of\n2026-11-04:\n\n- shell_quoted rendered the path through Path::display(), which replaces\n  bytes that are not UTF-8. An outside-root tamper could then meet ENOENT\n  on another pathname and pass the ABSENT check. It now writes one bash\n  $'...' word: printable ASCII other than a quote or a backslash stands as\n  itself, and every other byte is \\xHH. A new control,\n  a_quoted_path_that_is_not_utf8_names_its_own_bytes, plants the lossy\n  name beside the real one and fails under the old quoting.\n- The quoting control ran host bash with -lc, so a login profile could\n  change PATH or define cat. It now runs bash -c with the cleared\n  environment. The box itself still runs bash -lc, under its own private\n  HOME.\n\nshell_quoted and its controls move to hands/tests/quoted.rs, since\nevidence.rs sat at the 2000-line test ceiling (now 1974). No production\ncode changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Valentin Yanakiev <redacted@example.invalid>","timestamp":"2026-11-21T09:44:01Z","author":{"name":"Valentin Yanakiev","email":"redacted@example.invalid"},"committer":{"name":"Valentin Yanakiev","email":"redacted@example.invalid"}},"repository":{"id":1342197582,"node_id":"R_kgDOUABPTg","name":"brokkr","full_name":"feedback-loop-ai/brokkr","private":false,"owner":{"login":"feedback-loop-ai","id":250017135,"node_id":"O_kgDODub1bw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250017135?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feedback-loop-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/feedback-loop-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feedback-loop-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feedback-lo